🔴 Issue 1: Mutated request is NOT applied

This line:

exchange.mutate().request(
    exchange.getRequest().mutate()
        .header("X-Logged-In-User", username)
        .build())
    .build();


👉 You are mutating, but NOT using the mutated exchange.

❌ The downstream service will NOT receive the header.

🔴 Issue 2: Token validated but roles not propagated

You validate the token but:

You don’t pass role / authorities

Downstream services can’t do authorization properly

🟡 Issue 3: Gateway doing too much logging at INFO

This line:

log.info("ACCESS GRANTED: User [{}] authorized for request to [{}]", username, ...)


In high-traffic systems:

This should be DEBUG

INFO logs are for business events, not every request

🟡 Issue 4: Missing response body for 401

Right now, clients get:

HTTP 401

No message

Good APIs return structured errors.

